WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.900
What's a super hexagon?

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.580
Does it really help us remember all the trigonometric formulae

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.580
and identities we have seen so far?

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.520
Yes it does. It's a simple hexagon

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.400
which looks like this.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.260
All we need to do is join all the opposite vertices

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.160
and that gives us three diagonals.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.220
We write the number one in the center.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.680
It's still difficult to believe that one hexagon

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.360
can lead us to so many formulae.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.820
To know the formulae, we give the six

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.400
function names to each of the six vertices.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.900
But there is a particular way in which we need to write it.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.920
We start writing from this vertex,

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.920
go around the hexagon

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.920
and end at this one.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.560
It's simple! We just draw a hexagon

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.480
join its opposite vertices and write a 1 in the center.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.220
Now let's see,

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.820
how we write the six functions at the six vertices.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.560
We just need to remember

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.620
one formula which we have already seen.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.960
tan is equal to sine by cos.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.880
We have used this formula like a zillion times now.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.200
tan is equal to sine by cos.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:23.460
We start at this vertex and write tan, sine, cos

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.560
in the clockwise direction.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.720
tan, sine, cos.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:32.340
Now three functions and three vertices
remain.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.360
We write cot opposite to tan.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:39.360
Remember co-tangent opposite to tangent.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.200
What remains is cosec and sec.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.300
If we draw a vertical line through the center of the hexagon,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.100
we will have three vertices

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.700
on the left and three on the right.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.900
So to remember what's written on this vertex

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.760
just remember that we have all functions

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.980
starting with c on the right side.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.080
So we write a cosec here and what remains is sec.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.160
That's all you need to remember

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.180
about how the super-hex has to be drawn.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.680
Three diagonals joining the opposite

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.410
vertices, the number one in the centre
and the six function

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.180
at the vertices.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.580
So let's draw the super-hex on a new page.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.740
A hexagon with three diagonals joining the opposite vertices.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.960
The number one at the centre,

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:35.320
tan is equal to sign by cos, cot opposite to tan

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.900
cosec here since all c's are on the right

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.700
and what remains is sec.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.600
Are you ready?

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.480
You're going to learn a whole set

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.560
of trigonometric formulae.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.120
This video is fun but also very long as we will be

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.740
covering most of the trigonometric formulae we have studied before.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.220
To understand the first set of formulae

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.600
let's try going around the hexagon in

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.460
the clockwise fashion.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.460
We go like this.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.180
This tells us that tan theta equals sine

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.480
theta by cos theta.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:14.140
Well that's how we started making our hexagon.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.540
Now lets see the next three functions in clockwise direction.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.820
These three!

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.140
This tells us that

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.720
sine theta equals cos theta by cot theta

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.720
The first one equals the second one by

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.180
the third one.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.000
Take the next three functions clockwise.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.020
First equals second by third.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.320
Hence cos theta equals cot theta by cosec theta.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.620
And if we take the

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.120
next three functions, we can say

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.320
that cot theta equals cosec theta by sec theta.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.480
And we will get two more formulae if we go clockwise.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.700
Cosec is equal to sec by tan.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.360
And sec is equal to tan by sine.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:05.360
Wasn't that simple? One hexagon and six

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.080
formulae without any effort.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.980
Great! But what if you forget that you had to go

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.440
clockwise and you go anti-clockwise instead.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.500
Let's say you started like this, in the anti clockwise direction.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:23.420
Don't worry! The pattern still holds true.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:26.440
First will equal second by third.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.680
tan theta equals sec theta by cosec theta.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.640
First equals second by third.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:37.400
If we take these three functions anti-clockwise,

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.920
we can write sine theta equals tan theta by sec theta.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.240
If these three, then cos theta equals sine theta

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.700
by tan theta and the list goes on.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.380
Whether you go anti-clockwise or clockwise,

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.340
first will always equal second by third.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.660
We can easily get three more here.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.480
One simple hexagon and twelve formulae.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.000
Is that all? No, there's more!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.420
Let's draw the super-hex on a new page to understand

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.100
what else there is!

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:17.320
We draw the super-hex and write a 1 in the centre.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.520
tan is equal to sine by cos,

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.900
cot opposite to tan,

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.240
as we have all c's on the right, we write a

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.940
cosec here and what remains is sec.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.940
In the previous set of formulae we did not use the one

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.540
which was written in the centre.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.820
Let's see why it is placed like this.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.880
If we multiply the functions at the opposite vertices,

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.880
we get a 1.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.080
This multiplied by this equals 1.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:52.900
sine theta multiplied by cosec theta equals 1.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.780
This multiplied by this also gives us 1.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:06:00.780
cos theta multiplied by sec theta equals 1.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.820
And this multiplied by this also equals 1.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:10.380
tan theta multiplied by cot theta equals 1.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.160
So when functions are diagonally opposite vertices are multiplied,

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:19.760
we get a 1. Wait, there's more.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.220
We draw the super-hex, right the number

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.980
one at the center.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.960
tan equals sine by cos, cot opposite to tan

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:35.180
and cosec here since all c's have to be on the right

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:38.000
and what remains is sec.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.680
I repeat the positions again and again

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.660
so it gets etched in your brain

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.600
after watching the video.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.280
Take any three continuous functions in the hexagon

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:51.040
like tan, sine and cos.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.760
tan multiplied by cos will give us sine.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.780
So if three continuous functions are taken

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:01.120
the product of the first and the third functions result in

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.520
the function in between them.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:07.720
We can say that tan theta multiplied by cos theta

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.980
equals sine theta.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.000
Take these three functions for example.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:16.540
This multiplied by this will give cosec.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:22.620
So sec theta multiplied by cot theta will give us cosec theta.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:27.320
Even cot multiplied by sine will give us cos.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:32.340
cosec multiplied by tan will give us sec and so on.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.000
First term multiplied by the third term

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.440
will give us the term in between them.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.920
Does it end here? Not yet.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:44.200
Let's redraw the hexagon with one in the center.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:49.740
tan is equal to sine by cos, cot opposite to tan,

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:53.080
cosec here as all c's on the right

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.780
and what remains is sec.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.260
Now focus on the functions at

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.440
diagonally opposite vertices.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:06.520
sine and cosec, cos and sec, cot and tan.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.940
They are reciprocals of each other.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.780
Look at this arrow for instance.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.660
This arrow tells us that sine theta equals one by cosec theta.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.600
What about this arrow?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:25.120
This arrow tells us that cos theta is one by sec theta.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.860
And this arrow tells us that

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:31.180
cot theta equals 1 by tan theta.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:35.340
If the arrow is drawn like this, we can even say

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:39.320
that cosec theta is reciprocal of sine theta.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:40.660
So remember.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.400
Functions at diagonally opposite vertices

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.640
are reciprocals of each other.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.460
Be patient, it doesn't end here.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.760
But let's review what we have covered so far.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:58.300
This equals this by this. Or this equals this by this.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:03.000
This multiplied by this equals 1 or this multiplied by

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.940
this equals 1.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:10.060
This multiplied by this equals this and this is equal to

00:09:10.060 --> 00:09:12.080
reciprocal of this.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:17.180
Let's draw the super hex again to know the other stuff it tell us.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:23.020
tan is equal to sine by cos, cot opposite to tan

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.960
cosec here as all c's are on the right hand side

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.160
and the remaining function sec here.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.120
Do you remember complementary angles?

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.700
Yes two angles are complementary if their sum

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.580
equals 90 degrees.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:42.280
And the trigonometric functions had a special relation

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.520
with complementary angles.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.940
Look at this arrow. What does it tell us about sin and cos?

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:52.340
It tells us that sin of theta equals.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.680
cos of 90 degrees minus theta.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.880
This horizontal arrow tells us that sin of an angle

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.860
is equal to the cosine of its

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.840
complementary angle.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.040
Similarly this arrow tells us that tan theta

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:11.340
equals cot of 90 degrees minus theta.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:16.440
And this arrow tells us that sec theta equals cosec 90

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.280
degrees minus theta.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:22.560
And if the arrow is drawn this way it will tell us that cos

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:27.080
of theta equals sin of 90 degrees minus theta.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.140
So a horizontal arrow tells us

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:31.980
that one function of an angle

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.220
is equal to the other function of its

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.120
complementary angle.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:40.380
I think I have lost track of how many formulae

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:44.200
the super hex has helped us remember and there's more.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.900
This is the super hexagon with a 1 in the center.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.800
tan is equal to sign by cos, cot opposite to tan,

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.020
cosec is written here as we have all the C's on the right hand side,

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:01.640
and the only remaining function sec is written here.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.000
Look at the figure.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.760
There are six triangles formed inside.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:12.080
Focus on three. This one, this one and this one.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.460
Let's zoom out slightly.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:19.180
Okay, so here we go clockwise within each of the

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:22.440
triangles starting with top left position.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:26.460
Like this, sine, cos and one.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.220
This gives us one very important identity.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:34.640
This squared plus this squared equals this squared.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:40.640
So sine squared theta plus cos squared theta equals one.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.820
Now let's go clockwise in this triangle.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.300
This squared plus this squared will

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.080
equal this square.

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:53.500
One plus cot squared theta will equal cosec squared theta.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.980
If we go clockwise in this triangle

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.620
we get tan squared theta plus one equals

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.240
sec squared theta.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:06.420
Amazing, Isn't it? This arrow can also be

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:10.960
drawn anti-clockwise from the bottom of the triangle like this.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.780
The only difference with anti-clockwise is that

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:17.020
there will be a minus sign before the second term.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:22.360
So it will be this squared minus this squared equals this squared.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:26.200
So we can say that 1 minus cos squared theta

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.480
will equal sine squared theta.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:32.700
Similarly if these two also became anti-clockwise,

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.980
we get two more results.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:39.920
cosec squared theta minus cot squared theta equals 1.

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:45.900
And sec squared theta minus 1 equals tan squared theta.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.540
Now you know why we call it super.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:54.260
One hexagon helped us with so many formulae in trigonometry.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:56.300
But hang on you have to

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:58.380
practice this procedure well.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.360
Because there are a few things you need to

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.220
remember here too.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.640
The position of the functions, the

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.700
directions of arrows and so on.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:11.180
This video is not a substitute for all the

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.320
other videos done before this.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.520
It's just an add on.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.520
Memorizing formulae can never

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:19.200
be the solution.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.040
Make sure you understand all the formulae

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.900
we derived in the previous videos.

